                        <handDesc>
                            <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                                <seg type="script" cert="medium">Eighteenth or nineteenth-century script (?). Liqe Zämäläkot is mentioned as the scribe in the explicit of the “History of the Oromo people” (f. 33rb). It is very likely, however, that he was the composer of the work and not the scribe of the manuscript</seg>
                                <seg type="ink">Black, red.</seg>                                
                                <seg type="rubrication">Groups of lines in the incipit page of text I (f. 3r); two incipit lines of text II (f. 33rb); holy names; elements of the punctuation signs and numerals</seg>
                            </handNote>
                        </handDesc>
                        <decoDesc>
